/*
Detection Rule: AWS Cross-Account Role Assumption Chaining
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1548.005 - Abuse Elevation Control: Temporary Elevated Cloud Access
              T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
Severity: High
Description: Detects role assumption chains where a principal assumes one role
then uses that role to assume another — especially across account boundaries.
Attackers use chaining to pivot from a low-privilege initial foothold to a
highly privileged role in a target account while obscuring the original identity.
This rule flags 3 or more AssumeRole calls within a 10-minute window, or any
AssumedRole-type principal making cross-account role assumptions.
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    eventName="AssumeRole"
    errorCode=""

| eval actor=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
| eval actor_account=userIdentity.accountId
| eval actor_type=userIdentity.type
| eval assumed_role_arn=requestParameters.roleArn
| eval session_name=requestParameters.roleSessionName
| eval assumed_account=mvindex(split(assumed_role_arn, ":"), 4)

| eval is_cross_account=if(actor_account!=assumed_account, 1, 0)

/* Aggregate over 10-minute windows to catch rapid chaining */
| bin _time span=10m
| stats
    count                        AS assume_count,
    dc(assumed_role_arn)         AS distinct_roles,
    dc(assumed_account)          AS distinct_accounts,
    values(assumed_role_arn)     AS roles_assumed,
    values(assumed_account)      AS target_accounts,
    values(session_name)         AS session_names,
    values(sourceIPAddress)      AS source_ips,
    sum(is_cross_account)        AS cross_account_hops,
    min(_time)                   AS first_seen,
    max(_time)                   AS last_seen
    by actor, actor_type, actor_account, _time

| where assume_count >= 3 OR (cross_account_hops >= 1 AND actor_type="AssumedRole")

/* Score based on chain depth, account spread, and actor type */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(assume_count >= 5 AND distinct_accounts >= 2,  risk_score+60, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(assume_count >= 3 AND distinct_accounts >= 2,  risk_score+40, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(cross_account_hops >= 1 AND actor_type="AssumedRole", risk_score+35, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(assume_count >= 3 AND distinct_accounts < 2,   risk_score+20, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(session_names, "^[a-z0-9]{8,}$"),        risk_score+10, risk_score)

| eval alert_title="Role Assumption Chain Detected: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, actor_type, actor_account,
        assume_count, distinct_roles, distinct_accounts,
        roles_assumed, target_accounts, session_names,
        cross_account_hops, source_ips, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- assume_count threshold: Raise to 5 in large environments with complex CI/CD pipelines
- cross_account_hops: Remove the AssumedRole condition if your org uses federated roles heavily
- Time window span: Widen to 30m if your pipelines perform sequential role assumptions slowly
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(actor, "CodePipeline|GitHubActions|JenkinsRole|TerraformCloud")
  | where NOT match(assumed_role_arn, "arn:aws:iam::<known-mgmt-account>")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- CI/CD pipelines assuming multiple roles for multi-environment deployments (dev→staging→prod)
- AWS Organizations management account tools reading across member accounts
- Security tooling (Config aggregator, Security Hub, GuardDuty master) performing multi-account reads
- AWS SSO/IAM Identity Center session vending across accounts

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Map the full assumption chain — trace actor → role1 → role2 → final target role
2. Identify the originating identity and confirm it is authorized for cross-account access
3. Determine what API actions were performed under each assumed role session
4. If confirmed malicious: revoke all STS tokens via aws sts revoke-session
5. Restrict the abused role's trust policy to specific, approved source ARNs
6. Audit all API activity across every account in the chain for data access or changes

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- Full session API calls: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.principalId=<actor> earliest=<first_seen> latest=<last_seen>
  | table _time, eventName, awsRegion, sourceIPAddress, requestParameters
- Actions under final assumed role: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn=<final_role_arn> earliest=-2h
  | table _time, eventName, requestParameters
- Session name analysis: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  eventName="AssumeRole" requestParameters.roleSessionName=<session_name>
  | table _time, userIdentity.arn, requestParameters.roleArn, sourceIPAddress

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail (management events) — all regions and all accounts in the organization

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Session names are generic (random strings, timestamps) rather than descriptive pipeline names
- Final assumed role has AdministratorAccess or IAMFullAccess
- Source IP changes between assumption hops (attacker relaying through compromised instances)
- Assumptions occur outside normal business hours for the originating account

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Add aws:PrincipalArn conditions to role trust policies to restrict assumption sources
- Enable STS regional endpoints and disable global STS endpoint where possible
- Set maximum session duration on roles to limit the window of stolen token validity
- Implement AWS Config rule to alert on new cross-account trust relationships

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
- T1550.001 - Use Alternate Authentication Material: Application Access Token
- T1619 - Cloud Storage Object Discovery

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
